---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **영화와 시리즈는 다르게 버틴다.** (`/run-length`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   /exit 에서 「어느 자리에서 나가나」를 재면서 **영화와 시리즈를 안 갈랐다.**
 *   둘은 버티는 방식이 다를 수밖에 없다 — 시리즈는 다음 회가 오고 영화는 안 온다.
 *   ⭐ 갈라 보니 **한국 영화는 남의 영화와 사실상 같고, 한국 시리즈만 길었다.**
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **「한국이 오래 간다」로 뭉뚱그리지 않는다.** 갈래 차이를 뺀 나머지를 따로 낸다.
 * ⛔ **평균 하나로 안 말한다.** 가장 큰 작품을 뺀 값을 나란히 둔다 —
 *    오늘 /fewer-titles 에서 「머리가 두꺼워졌다」가 실은 한 편이었다.
 * ⛔ 아직 안 끝난 구간은 길이를 모른다. 빼고 세고 **몇 개를 뺐는지 화면에 적는다.**
 * ⛔ 작품을 줄세우지 않는다. 이름을 안 적는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 * ⚠ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `wikitip-run-length.json` 에서 읽는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-run-length.json';

const 찾 = (g) => d.byGroup.find((x) => x.group === g);
const 한영 = 찾('한국 영화'); const 한시 = 찾('한국 시리즈');
const 밖영 = 찾('그 밖 영화'); const 밖시 = 찾('그 밖 시리즈');
const 영어이름 = {
  '한국 영화': 'Korean films',
  '한국 시리즈': 'Korean series',
  '그 밖 영화': 'Every other film',
  '그 밖 시리즈': 'Every other series',
};
const 차례 = ['한국 영화', '그 밖 영화', '한국 시리즈', '그 밖 시리즈'].map(찾);
const 총구간 = d.byGroup.reduce((s, g) => s + g.runs, 0);
const 총잘림 = d.byGroup.reduce((s, g) => s + g.truncated, 0);

const TITLE = 'How long a Korean title holds a chart — films against series';
const DESC =
  `Across ${총구간.toLocaleString('en-US')} finished runs, a Korean film holds a country top 10 for `
  + `${한영.meanWeeks} weeks on average and every other film for ${밖영.meanWeeks}. Korean series run `
  + `${한시.meanWeeks} weeks against ${밖시.meanWeeks}. The staying power is entirely in the series.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/run-length">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Korean films <b>{한영.meanWeeks}</b> weeks · every other film <b>{밖영.meanWeeks}</b> —
    the same. Korean series <b>{한시.meanWeeks}</b> · every other series <b>{밖시.meanWeeks}</b>.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Four groups, measured the same way</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th></th><th>Runs</th><th>Median weeks</th><th>Mean weeks</th>
            <th>Gone after one week</th><th>Lasting 4+ weeks</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {차례.map((g) => (
            <tr class={g.group.startsWith('한국') ? 'edge' : undefined}>
              <td class="nm">{영어이름[g.group]}</td>
              <td>{g.runs.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td>{g.medianWeeks}</td>
              <td class="tot">{g.meanWeeks}</td>
              <td>{g.oneWeekPc}%</td>
              <td>{g.fourPlusPc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>{d.unit}</b></p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>{d.whyNonKoreanToo}</b>
    </p>
    <p class="note fine">
      {d.whyTruncatedRemoved} That is {총잘림.toLocaleString('en-US')} runs out of{' '}
      {(총구간 + 총잘림).toLocaleString('en-US')}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The part that is actually Korean</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th></th><th>Series minus films, mean weeks</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="nm">Korean titles</td><td class="tot">{d.formatGapKorean} weeks</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="nm">Every other title</td><td class="tot">{d.formatGapOthers} weeks</td></tr>
          <tr class="edge"><td class="nm">Difference</td><td class="tot">{d.formatGapDifference} weeks</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Series outlast films everywhere, so most of the gap between the two Korean rows above is the
      difference between formats rather than anything about Korea. Korean series pull away from
      Korean films by <b>{d.formatGapDifference} weeks more</b> than other series pull away from
      other films. That is the part left over, and it sits entirely on the series side.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>One title could have done this. It did not.</h2>
    <p class="body">
      {d.whyOneTitleCheck ?? 'A mean moves easily with a handful of very long runs. Each group is therefore measured again with its single most-charting title removed.'}
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th></th><th>Mean weeks</th><th>Without the biggest title</th>
            <th>4+ weeks</th><th>Without the biggest title</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[한시, 밖시, 한영, 밖영].map((g) => (
            <tr class={g.group.startsWith('한국') ? 'edge' : undefined}>
              <td class="nm">{영어이름[g.group]}</td>
              <td>{g.meanWeeks}</td>
              <td class="tot">{g.meanWeeksWithoutBiggest}</td>
              <td>{g.fourPlusPc}%</td>
              <td class="tot">{g.fourPlusPcWithoutBiggest}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The gap narrows and stays. We do not name the removed titles — the point is that no single one
      of them is carrying the result, not which one it was.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How they leave</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Of Korean series runs that ended, <b>{한시.exitBottomThreePc}%</b> ended from positions 8, 9 or
      10 — against {밖시.exitBottomThreePc}% for other series and {한영.exitBottomThreePc}% for Korean
      films. A Korean series is on the chart longer and then slides off the bottom of it; a Korean
      film is more often simply gone.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      And they are not sitting low to begin with: Korean series spend{' '}
      <b>{한시.weeksBottomThreePc}%</b> of their chart weeks in the bottom three positions against{' '}
      {밖시.weeksBottomThreePc}% for other series. They climb, hold, and then slide.
      {' '}<a href="/exit">How a title leaves</a> has the whole position table.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How this was counted, and what it cannot say</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source</b> — {d.source}</li>
      <li><b>Rows read</b> — {d.rowsRead.toLocaleString('en-US')}; {d.rowsOverwritten} rows could not
        be resolved to a single run and are reported rather than hidden.</li>
      <li><b>Films and series are separate charts.</b> Netflix publishes a films top 10 and a TV top
        10 for each country and week, so each has exactly one place at every position and neither
        crowds the other.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="warn">{d.cannotAnswer}</p>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/exit">How a title leaves</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/staying-power">Staying power and force</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/screen-split">Korea exports television, not film</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/run-length" />
</WikiTip>
